---
import config from '../config.json';
import { content, threads } from '../lib/content.ts';

/*
 * WHAT THIS SECTION REPLACED (2026-11-03). It used to be six cards with checkmarks — "Expert Guidance",
 * "Collaborative Learning", "Regular Meetups", "Study Resources", "Diverse Community", "Growth Mindset" —
 * under "Why Join Our Math Book Club? / Discover the benefits of collaborative learning and mathematical
 * exploration". Not one of those sentences came from `src/content.json`, from a source, or from the club:
 * "Learn from experienced mathematicians and educators", "Access to curated learning materials, problem
 * sets, and recommended readings" and "Monthly in-person study sessions" describe services this club does
 * not offer. The operator on the same day: the page has "no humanity", it is "too professional", and on
 * whether the club has ever written anything — "Our club has not written anything." All of it is now on the
 * retired list in `scripts/check-content.mjs`, so pasting a template's benefit grid back in fails the build.
 *
 * WHAT IS HERE INSTEAD, AND WHY IT IS UNDATED (operator ruling, 2026-11-03): "I don't want the home page to
 * give anyone an idea that our groups interests are as narrow as what we have done historically, so I don't
 * want to name enough specific things to give enough information to allow a pattern to emerge." A reading
 * list is exactly such a pattern-maker: nine titles with dates on them let a stranger infer the shape of the
 * club's past and predict its future. So this is a set of open threads, not an archive — no dates, no
 * authors, no titles, no sequence, and no row of past topics. A thread that goes quiet gets edited out of
 * `src/content.json` rather than kept as a record. `threads._rule` in that file is the authority; this
 * comment is where the shape of it is visible to whoever edits the markup.
 *
 * The strings come from `src/content.json` (source: the operator's account of the club's Discord channel,
 * 2026-11-03), so a non-developer can add or drop a thread from a phone without touching markup. An item
 * with no `value` is a hole and renders nothing rather than a bracket (record 0010).
 *
 * The file name stays `WhyJoinUs.astro`: the section is still the answer to "why would I come", and the
 * design tooling (`design/gen-token-map.mjs`, `design/ratify-check.mjs`, `design/audit-references.mjs`)
 * names this path. Renaming it is a separate change with its own reference sweep.
 */
const items = threads();
---

<section class="bg-panel py-16">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-measure">
      <h2 class="text-heading font-extrabold text-ink">
        What we take up
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lede leading-prose text-ink-2 font-body">
        Threads that are open in the club's chat. This is not a syllabus and there is nothing to keep up
        with: any of them can be dropped mid-sentence, the list changes when the chat changes, and none of
        them is a prerequisite for the others.
      </p>
    </div>

    {items.length > 0 && (
      // No hairlines between the rows, on purpose, and that is a measurement rather than a taste: the render
      // gate fails a painted 1px line that is a border/outline instead of the ratified inset ring
      // (`inset-shadow-rule`), and on this section's `bg-panel` ground `--color-rule` measures 2.88 — under
      // the 3.0 graphic bar it is solved to hit on paper (3.01). Rows sit on 12px padding (DESIGN.md,
      // Spacing) and the label/gloss weight difference does the grouping the rule was going to do.
      <ul class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-12 md:grid-cols-2">
        {items.map(({ label, gloss }) => (
          <li class="py-3 text-body leading-prose font-body">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink">{label}</span>
            {gloss && <span class="text-ink-2"> — {gloss}</span>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )}

    {items.length === 0 && (
      // record 0010: a hole is a designed state, never a blank. If every thread slot is empty the section
      // says so and hands the reader the path where threads actually live.
      //
      // The edge is GOLD here, and that is a ground measurement rather than a colour preference. This section
      // paints `bg-panel`, and `--color-rule` on a tint measures **2.88** - under the 3.0 graphic bar it is
      // solved to clear on paper (3.01), and 2.74 on `tint` (design/records/0018-a-hairline-on-a-tint-is-under-
      // its-own-bar.md). D149-3c ruled that a keyline may not straddle two grounds and that the fix is the
      // placement, not the number; here there is no paper to move the box onto, because the whole section is a
      // tint. So this is the state DESIGN.md's caution grammar exists for: `inset-shadow-gold` with a gold
      // word, 4.61 on panel and 4.82 on paper, both over the 4.5 text bar. The state genuinely is a caution:
      // an empty list is a fact about this page's wiring, not about the club, and the sentence says exactly
      // that. `check:render` asserts every inset ring's pair, so if this branch ever renders it is measured.
      <div class="mt-8 inset-shadow-gold rounded-control px-4 py-3 max-w-measure">
        <p class="text-body font-medium text-gold">Nothing is on the list right now.</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-body leading-prose text-ink-2">
          What the club is pulling on is decided in its chat, so an empty list here means the page has not
          been told yet, not that the club is quiet.
        </p>
      </div>
    )}

    <p class="mt-12 max-w-measure text-body leading-prose text-ink-2 font-body">
      Dates and places go up on{' '}
      <a
        class="underline hover:text-gold"
        href={config.URLs.meetupGroup}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Meetup</a>, where the sign-up is. One evening is enough to tell whether this is your kind of room.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
